  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$20$ is less than $10$ **or** $4$ divides $18.$\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $S:20\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}10$\n\n- $R:4\\text{\u00a0divides\u00a0}18$\n\nExpressed in symbolic form, our statement can be written as\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{20\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}10}_{\u23df}}_{S}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{4\\text{\u00a0divides\u00a0}18}_{\u23df}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $S\u2228R.$",
